body:
Schema-driven action buttons in the list view toolbar (`action:bar` with `locations: ['list_toolbar']`) were rendered via `SchemaRenderer` without an `ActionProvider` ancestor. `useAction()` fell back to a throwaway local `ActionRunner` with no handlers — clicks executed silently.

### Changes

- **`apps/console/src/components/ObjectView.tsx`** — Wrapped the component tree with `ActionProvider`, mirroring the existing pattern in `RecordDetailView`:
  - `onConfirm` → `ActionConfirmDialog` (promise-based)
  - `onToast` → Sonner
  - `onNavigate` → React Router / `window.open`
  - `onParamCollection` → `ActionParamDialog`
  - `handlers.api` → generic `dataSource.execute()` fallback

- **`apps/console/src/__tests__/ListToolbarActions.test.tsx`** — 4 integration tests: renders buttons, shows confirm dialog on click, executes on accept, skips on cancel.

- **`CHANGELOG.md`** — Documented fix.

### Before / After

```tsx
// Before — action:bar rendered without ActionProvider context
<SchemaRenderer schema={{
  type: 'action:bar',
  location: 'list_toolbar',
  actions: objectDef.actions,
}} />
// useAction() → new ActionRunner() with no handlers → silent no-op

// After — ActionProvider wraps the tree
<ActionProvider
  context={{ objectName: objectDef.name, user: currentUser }}
  onConfirm={confirmHandler}
  onToast={toastHandler}
  onNavigate={navigateHandler}
  onParamCollection={paramCollectionHandler}
  handlers={{ api: apiHandler }}
>
  {/* ... existing content including action:bar ... */}
</ActionProvider>
```

